0'' oven -> /about, /services", "Stainless steel and aluminum fabrication with polishing/re-graining -> /about", "On-site repair of stainless restaurant equipment -> /about", "Custom aluminum truck beds -> /about, /services", "Services list: welding, fabrication, control rooms, consoles, workstations, mobile repair, truck beds, powder coating, trailers, security products, enclosures, CNC parts, handrails, obsolete parts, polishing, tube bending, TIG welding, CNC punching, plasma cutting, oxy-acetylene cutting, brake press forming -> /services", "Guarantee to make it right -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our goal is to be a one stop shop for all of your metal fabrication needs. With an array of CNC controlled equipment and skilled craftsmen we can take your project from paper to finished product on time, on budget, and with results you won''t get anywhere else.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='fabtech-custom-metal-fabrication-welding' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Factor 55 is based in Boise, Idaho. The company began as an engineering design firm whose staff brought extensive experience from the aerospace, defense, and semiconductor sectors, applying that rigor to a shared passion for off-road vehicle recovery.

Factor 55 designs and manufactures a line of recovery hardware including winch-line shackle mounts (UltraHook, FlatLink, ProLink), vehicle recovery kits (Owyhee, Sawtooth, Borah, Baja), kinetic recovery ropes, and a range of rigging accessories. Products are developed in-house using 3D CAD and Cosmos finite-element analysis, then validated through destructive testing at an instrumented test facility. Components are precision CNC-machined from 6000- and 7000-series aluminum alloys and 6Al-4V titanium.

The gear serves recreational off-road drivers (Jeep, truck, SUV), powersports users (UTV, ATV), and military/industrial customers. Example product families include the UltraHook XTV for side-by-sides, the FlatLink MultiMount for winch mounting, and the HD Recovery Kit Teton for heavy-duty trucks.

The company differentiates itself through its Closed System Winching™ methodology, which replaces traditional hooks with closed-link hardware to eliminate latch failure.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Mechanical design and analysis", "3D CAD modeling", "Finite Element Analysis (FEA)", "Destructive testing", "CNC machining", "Product development", "Closed System Winching methodology", "Recovery gear manufacturing"], "industries": ["Off-road vehicle recovery", "Powersports (UTV/ATV)", "Military", "Industrial", "Automotive aftermarket"], "materials": ["7000 series aluminum", "6000 series aluminum", "6Al-4V titanium (Grade 5)"], "equipment": ["CNC machining centers", "Cosmos FEA software", "Test measurement and data recording equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Closed System Winching\u2122 closed-link rigging technique", "In-house 3D CAD design with Cosmos FEA optimization", "Destructive testing of every design before release", "Precision CNC machining of military-grade aluminum and aerospace-grade titanium", "Engineering team with aerospace, defense, and semiconductor background"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Boise, Idaho -> /about-us", "Engineering design firm with aerospace/defense/semiconductor experience -> /about-us", "In-house 3D CAD and Cosmos FEA -> /about-us", "Destructive testing of each design -> /about-us", "Closed System Winching methodology -> /", "Product lines: UltraHook, FlatLink, ProLink, recovery kits -> /", "Materials: 6000/7000 series aluminum, 6Al-4V titanium -> /", "Industries served: off-road, powersports, military/industrial -> /", "CNC machining -> /", "Test facility with measurement equipment -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "All of our products are designed in house using the latest 3D CAD software and optimized using Cosmos FEA (Finite Element Analysis). Before we release any products to the public, we also perform a destructive test on each design with the assistance of a test facility equipped with test measurement and data recording equipment.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='factor-55' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Factory Connection is headquartered in Prattville, Alabama. The company was founded in 1976 in Guntersville, Alabama, by Terry Scott and Kenny Littleton as a single 1,000-square-foot store. It remains family-owned and is now led by President and CEO Steve Williams alongside a team of executive managers, merchandisers, buyers, and regional and store personnel.

The retailer operates more than 200 stores across 16 states, encompassing over one million square feet of retail space. A state-of-the-art distribution center at the Guntersville corporate headquarters supports the network, enabling frequent shipment of new merchandise — often from limited-quantity purchases. Factory Connection buys from fashion manufacturers to offer brand-name and specialty-store apparel for juniors, misses, plus, men’s, accessories, shoes, and home décor at prices 25% to 70% below regular retail.

The chain serves consumers in small to medium-sized markets throughout Alabama, Arkansas, Georgia, Illinois, Indiana, Kentucky, Kansas, Louisiana, Missouri, Mississippi, Ohio, Oklahoma, Tennessee, Texas, Virginia, and West Virginia, with additional expansion states identified. Its customer base includes shoppers seeking affordable, current fashion in communities not typically served by large boutiques or department stores.

Factory Connection emphasizes its innovative buying process and strong relationships with major manufacturers as the foundation for making great fashion brands available and affordable for everyone. The company’s mission has centered on bringing the latest styles to smaller towns for more than 40 years.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Retail apparel sales", "Multi-store retail operations", "Distribution center management", "Merchandise buying and planning", "Inventory replenishment and allocation"], "industries": ["Apparel retail", "Fashion retail", "Consumer goods retail"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Brand-name fashions at 25\u201370% below regular retail prices", "Frequent new merchandise shipments, including limited-quantity buys", "State-of-the-art distribution center supporting 200+ stores", "Innovative buying process and strong manufacturer relationships", "Focus on small to medium-sized markets underserved by larger retailers"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Prattville, Alabama -> db", "Founded 1976 in Guntersville, Alabama by Terry Scott and Kenny Littleton -> /about-us", "Family-owned, led by CEO Steve Williams -> /about-us", "Over 200 stores across 16 states, >1 million sq ft retail space -> /about-us", "State-of-the-art distribution center at Guntersville corporate headquarters -> /about-us", "Buys from leading fashion manufacturers, offers 25-70% below retail -> /about-us", "Serves markets in 16 listed states -> /about-us", "Focus on small to medium-sized markets, innovative buying process -> /about-us", "Instagram @factoryconnection -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Factory Connection specializes in providing the latest fashion apparel for customers in small to medium size markets. With over 200 stores in 17 states and growing rapidly, Factory Connection is a destination shopping experience for many of our customers.", "founded_year": "1976", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.instagram.com/factoryconnection/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='factory-connection' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Fairhaven Furniture operates in New Haven, Connecticut, where it has been family-owned for two generations. The founding year and the names of the original founders are not disclosed in public materials.

The company functions as a furniture retailer, carrying brands such as Stressless and Stickley alongside other lines sourced from craftspeople in the United States, Scandinavia, and Italy. Its showroom covers living, dining, bedroom, and office categories, and it operates an outlet section for discounted floor models. Services include complimentary interior design consultation for residential projects, and interest-free financing for up to 12 months. No figures for facility size, headcount, or annual sales volume are published.

Fairhaven Furniture serves residential customers, including homeowners furnishing a single room or an entire house. The design service is positioned for both partial refreshes and whole-home projects. The brand mix emphasizes durability and craftsmanship, targeting buyers who prioritize long-lasting pieces over disposable furniture.

This focus on longevity and design integrity is presented as the core reason for the company''s existence.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Free interior design consultation", "Residential furniture retail", "Outlet clearance sales", "Interest-free financing (12 months)"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Home furnishings", "Interior design services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned for two generations", "Free interior design consultation", "Curated selection of U.S., Scandinavian, and Italian-made furniture", "Outlet section with discounted floor models", "Interest-free financing for 12 months"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in New Haven, Connecticut -> db", "Family-owned for two generations -> /", "Offers free design services -> /", "Carries brands such as Stressless and Stickley -> /", "Sells American-made furniture from U.S., Scandinavia, Italy -> /", "Operates an outlet with discounted floor models -> /", "Provides interest-free financing for 12 months -> /", "Serves residential customers for living, dining, bedroom, office furniture -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Fairhaven Furniture is not your average store \u2013 we''re a furniture store with a soul.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='fairhaven-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Falcon Fabricators Nashville operates from a 50,000-square-foot facility in Nashville, Tennessee. The company traces its roots to KFC Manufacturing and has spent over four decades in the food-service replacement-parts business. The plant is NSF compliant and houses a range of modern fabrication equipment.

The shop specializes in precision sheet metal work, offering laser cutting, plasma cutting, CNC punching, CNC press braking, and TIG, MIG, arc, and spot welding, backed by an experienced finishing department. Core products include 304-grade stainless-steel work tables, three- and four-compartment sinks, dish tables, sneeze guards, counter tops, rotary marinators, holding bins, and corn cookers. The company also fabricates custom metal parts for virtually any application.

Primary customers are food-service operators and restaurants, but the custom fabrication side serves businesses of all types. Falcon stocks replacement parts for brands such as Ayrking, Delfield, FryMaster, Henny Penny, Pitco, and Quality, and carries equipment like the CCF-16 shortening filtration machine, rotary meat marinators, and drop-in and counter-top corn cookers. In-stock parts ordered before noon ship the same day, with next-day and second-day air options.

