Niebuhr cradle feed spreading machines -> /", "Gerber Accumark for marking/grading -> /", "QuickBooks Enterprise and Lightspeed for inventory -> /", "Pick, pack, ship for online retail -> /", "Sample runs <100 pcs to large production runs -> /", "Industries: outerwear, home accessories, specialty items, medical products -> /", "Historical catalog/retail customers -> /", "All services in-house, Made in USA, no order too big or small -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our contract sewing facility uses the latest machinery and production techniques. All aspects of production will be in-house from piece goods receipt to cutting, sewing, and shipping.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "100+ (peak)", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='fall-river-apparel-mfg-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Fargo Apparel is based in Fargo, North Dakota. Public records do not disclose the company''s founding date, ownership model, or the names of its founders.

The company also produces promotional merchandise, flags, banners, and recognition awards such as medals and trophies. In addition to its own stock, Fargo Apparel will print or engrave on items supplied by the customer. The shop markets its services under the slogan "Custom Products Made Easy" and emphasizes variety with the tagline "More Than Just Shirts!".

The client base appears to include sports teams, corporate buyers of promotional goods, and individuals seeking personalized gifts. One testimonial on the company''s site references an order for "Nolan''s Crew t‑shirts," indicating work with organized groups. The range of products — from team uniforms to engraved awards — suggests the shop serves both organizational and retail‑oriented demand.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Screen printing", "Laser engraving", "Embroidery", "Custom apparel decoration", "Promotional product customization", "Engraving on customer-supplied items", "Printing on customer-supplied items", "Custom gift production", "Award and trophy production"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Company name and location -> db", "Screen printing, laser engraving, embroidery services -> /", "Product range: screen-printed apparel (shirts, hoodies, jerseys, polos, mittens), engraved gifts (cups, leather mittens), promotional items, flags, banners, awards, medals, trophies -> /", "Capability to print/engrave on customer-supplied items -> /", "Customer example: Nolan''s Crew t-shirts -> /", "Slogans: ''Custom Products Made Easy'', ''More Than Just Shirts!'' -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We offer a full line of screen printed apparel, medals, trophies, engraved gifts and promotional items.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='fargo-apparel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Fashion Tech Kansas City operates from Kansas City, Missouri, and was founded in 2010 by Laura Treas, who serves as founder and owner. Treas brought more than 16 years of experience in small-batch manufacturing and sewist training to the venture, which began as a way to help independent designers and inventors bring sewn products to market. The company later added the Artisan Small Batch Academy to address a shortage of skilled stitchers and to teach manufacturing-style sewing.

The shop provides end-to-end product development and no-minimum production for sewn goods. Services include prototyping, pattern making, sample creation, tech packs, grading, and materials sourcing, all handled in-house. A team of stitchers runs a full suite of machines capable of producing items ranging from lingerie to complex sewn inventions. The company also offers consulting and training for businesses that want to establish their own in-house sewing operations.

The company has worked on projects spanning lingerie, general sewn products, and product inventions, and it supports customers through design development, budgeting, and production workflow setup.

