ocated in downtown Winfield providing quilting supplies and offering longarm machine quilting.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='field-to-fabric-quilt-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Fiesta Plastics Inc. opened in 1988 in Mesa, Arizona, when founder Jack Thompson traded the title of his truck for a small injection molding machine after three decades in the plastics industry. Within months the machine was paid off and three more followed, laying the groundwork for a company that has grown steadily for over 30 years.

Today the 20,000-square-foot facility houses 19 injection molding machines ranging from 25 to 650 tons with shot sizes up to 7.5 pounds. The shop processes a wide range of thermoplastics including ABS, acetal, acrylic, HIPS, nylon, polycarbonate, polypropylene, polystyrene, polyurethane, PVC, and TPU. In-house tooling capabilities center on two Fadal high-speed machining centers, supporting mold production from simple mud sets to Class A tools, along with mold maintenance and repair.

The company serves customers needing a complete finished product, from micro-molded components to large complex assemblies. Its blog notes core competencies in mold building, injection molding, assembly, and value-added operations across a variety of part sizes and complexities.

Fiesta Plastics emphasizes a “Never Give Up” motto built on quality at an economical price, continual innovation, customer satisfaction as the top priority, and integrity in every interaction. The firm positions itself as a full-service partner rather than a molding shop alone, handling design, manufacturing, and delivery under one roof.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic Injection Molding", "Tooling and Machining", "High Speed Machining", "Mold Making", "Mold Maintenance and Repair", "Product Design", "Mold Design", "Reverse Engineering", "Rapid Prototyping (3D Printing)", "SolidWorks 2024 Design", "File Format Support (Part, STEP, IGES, STL)", "Assembly and Value-Added Operations"], "industries": [], "materials": ["ABS", "Acetal", "Acrylic", "HIPS", "Nylon", "Polycarbonate", "Polypropylene", "Polystyrene", "Polyurethane", "PVC", "TPU", "Metallic", "Elasto", "Acrylate", "Platinum", "Gold", "Sterling Silver", "Plated", "Brass", "Bronze", "Steel"], "equipment": ["19 Injection Molding Machines (Ostar, JSW, Mitsubishi, Jinhwa, Kawaguchi, Battenfeld) 25-650 ton", "2 Fadal High-Speed Tooling Centers", "3D Printers (for rapid prototyping)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "4-6 weeks from receipt of Purchase Order", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full-service from product design through finished delivery", "In-house tooling and machining with two Fadal high-speed centers", "19 injection molding machines covering 25\u2013650 ton range", "Mold maintenance and repair performed after every run", "Rapid prototyping via 3D printing in plastic and metal"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1988 by Jack Thompson -> /", "Location: Mesa, Arizona -> /", "20,000 sqft facility -> /", "19 molding machines 25-650 ton -> /", "Shot size up to 7.5 lbs -> /", "Materials list (ABS, Acetal, etc.) -> /", "Two Fadal tooling centers -> /", "Mold making from mud sets to Class A -> /", "Mold maintenance after every run -> /", "SolidWorks 2024 for design -> /", "Rapid prototyping with 3D printing -> /", "Lead times 4-6 weeks -> /", "Company motto and values -> /", "Full-service description -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Fiesta Plastics Inc. is not just a molding shop but instead a full service company. We specialize in designing, manufacturing and delivering a complete and finished product.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='fiesta-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Fine Wood Works is a family-owned cabinet shop based in Piedmont, Missouri. Founded in 2006 by Lucas and Sara Edgy, the business traces its roots to Lucas’s college years when he built bookcases and small cabinets for friends. By 2003 he was working full-time as a cabinetmaker in Piedmont, and two years later the couple opened Fine Wood Works. In 2006 they purchased 30 acres with a barn, which they remodeled into the current woodworking facility.

The company designs, builds, and installs custom cabinetry, furniture, architectural millwork, and front entrance systems for residential and commercial projects. Operating from an 11,000-square-foot shop expanded over the years — including a dedicated spray finishing room, sanding area, and countertop fabrication space — the team uses KCD software to create 3D cabinet presentations, a practice Lucas adopted early in the region. All work is completed in-house from design through installation.

Fine Wood Works serves homeowners undertaking kitchen, bathroom, and living-room remodels, as well as builders on new-home and commercial projects. Client testimonials reference projects in Town & Country, Missouri, and highlight collaboration with Lucas on custom islands, laundry rooms, and dining tables.

